{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>וידר</b> Three times in the Masorah: וידר יעקב · וידר ישראל · וידר יפתח. To teach that the righteous would make vows, and the first to make a vow was Jacob — this is \"that which he swore to YHWH, a vow to the Mighty One of Jacob.\" Why \"Mighty One of Jacob\"? Because he opened with vows first." "<b> ללבוש</b> Two times in the Masorah: here and the other ללבוש את הבגדים. Teaching that Jacob was High Priest, as stated in Beresheet Rabbah. HaShem said to Michael: You made My Jacob a blemished High Priest, limping on his thigh — by your life, you must be High Priest on high in his place. This is what is said: \"and gave me bread to eat and clothing to wear\" — that you should fulfill for me the priesthood I acquired from Esau, for the service was in the firstborn."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The unaddressed quotation \"that which he swore to YHWH, a vow to the Mighty One of Jacob\" is from Genesis 31:53; citation not present in the original.", 1 "The quotation ללבוש את הבגדים is from Exodus 29:30 (or Leviticus 8:7 in a variant reading); citation not present in the original. Beresheet Rabbah reference is to the midrashic work Beresheet Rabbah."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:22.113372015Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}